<div class="note"><p><strong>Why.</strong> The step landed at your approval of 11:53, in commit <code>23f18f024</code>. Commit <code>f1dff89b4</code> then made five changes, each by a decision of the coordinator's. “After each change lands” answers flag F1: in this skill a landing is a batch's. The landed section keeps every change since your last approval or your last word that you read the page, which answers flag F2: with only the last landing's changes, a change could land unseen while you are away. The publish by the page's URL answers flag F6: a worker given no URL makes a new page. The form of a landed item and the base of its diff answer flags F3 and F4: the diff base read two ways. The approved item's move to the landed changes answers flag F11, and the lint named by its path answers flag F5.</p></div>
